{
  "summary": "This experiment tested the effect of multiprofile aggregation via avgpool on the RNA-only, scvi_n200 configuration, directly comparable to the single-profile scvi_n200 baseline (llm_summary_003). The validation accuracy rose from ~52.0% to ~65.0% (F1 from ~49.8% to ~62.8%), a substantial ~13-point gain indicating that aggregating multiple profiles adds significant signal beyond a single profile and is a high-leverage axis of improvement, far exceeding the ~3.5-point encoder-quality gain observed earlier. It remains uncertain whether more complex aggregation strategies (e.g., transformer) could push beyond ~65%, whether this gain compounds with cross-modal fusion or alternative encoders, and whether the previously weak image modality might contribute more in a multiprofile context."
}

